# Blog Post Front Matter

All posts in `_posts/` follow this schema. Always generate front matter in this exact order:

```yaml
---
layout: post
title: "Title in quotes"
author: boyu
date: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS +0800
categories: [ PascalCase, PascalCase ]
tags: [ lowercase, lowercase ]
description: "SEO-friendly sentence describing the post."
image: /assets/images/headers/<slug>.<ext>
---
```

## Field Rules

- **layout**: always `post`, never omit
- **title**: always double-quoted
- **author**: always `boyu`
- **date**: `+0800` timezone offset (Hong Kong), use actual publish time not midnight
- **categories**: PascalCase, 1–2 values — e.g. `[ Tech, API ]`, `[ Journal, Thoughts ]`
- **tags**: all lowercase, 3–6 values — e.g. `[ tech, graphql, api, rest ]`
- **description**: double-quoted, 1–2 sentences, written for SEO
- **image**: path to `/assets/images/headers/<slug>.jpg` (or `.png`); omit only for casual journal posts
- Generate covers with `tools/cover-generator/` (1200×630 PNG preferred; JPG @ q100); see project conventions → Cover Image Generator

## Common Categories

| Track | Examples |
|-------|---------|
| Tech  | Tech, Java, API, Design, Demo, Agile |
| Life  | Journal, Thoughts, Life, Leadership |
| Music | Studio |

## Slug → Image Path

The image filename matches the post slug exactly:
- Post: `2026-02-27-graphql.md` → `image: /assets/images/headers/graphql.jpg`
- Post: `2026-02-10-solid-principle.md` → `image: /assets/images/headers/solid-principle.jpg`
